 hlp_msg db '²╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗',10
	db '║ Dear users! Thanks for choosing ²AUTOCONF.² You will not regret this choice!   ║',10
	db '║                                                                       D.D.   ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║    ²WHAT ²AUTOCONF² IS... ²                                                      ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² is a program, that allows you to choose a different configuration   ║',10
	db '║ of memory drivers, resident programs or other software you need in your      ║',10
	db '║ work or play.                                                                ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² is a very flexible program, adaptable to any individual need. It    ║',10    
	db '║ is definetely better than most of the simular existing programs.             ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║    ²WHY DOES ANYBODY NEED MULTIPLE CONFIGURATIONS?       ²                     ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ Have you aver had ''Insuffisent memory'' message? Your mouse driver is eating  ║',10
	db '║ 20k of precious memory and you need your mouse only once in a while.         ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ How many times per day do you edit your CONFIG.SYS file to add REMs in it?   ║',10
	db '║ Or worse, how many CONFIG.SYSs did you make, which you copy into the used one║',10
	db '║ to load the wanted configuration? How many boot disks lay scattered all over ║',10
	db '║ your table? Do you have so much time to loose? Enough!                       ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² is what you need!                       ²                            ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ You have now the PERFECT PROGRAM for multiple configurations in one and only ║',10
	db '║ CONFIG.SYS file and one and only AUTOEXEC.BAT! Il you are already using a    ║',10
	db '║ simular program, here is a little explanation of what ²AUTOCONF² does and the  ║',10
	db '║ most well known programs like Multiple configurations DOS 6.x, MBOOT 2.x or  ║',10
	db '║ LACE 1.x do not!                                                             ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² allows to create more than 200 different configuration, accessible  ║',10
	db '║ by a single key press: from A to Z, extended keys (ALT + key) or function    ║',10
	db '║ keys (F1...F10).                                                             ║',10 
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ This is the least important, since the greatest advantage is that ²AUTOCONF²   ║',10
	db '║ doesn''t need to stop your computer''s startup to allow you to choose a totally║',10
	db '║ different configuration: you just press a key BEFORE ²AUTOCONF² loads, right   ║',10
	db '║ after the little beep of your computer or the Starting MS DOS message, that  ║',10
	db '║ designates the wanted configuration!                                         ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ What you find in simular software is a poor uncolored menu, which forces you ║',10
	db '║ to choose a configuration. In a better case, a default configuration is      ║',10
	db '║ loaded in case you don''t press a key. Choosing a configuration with ²AUTOCONF² ║',10
	db '║ is as simple as pressing one single key! No more time to loose at all!       ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ You can create sub groups of configurations, acessible from the list of      ║',10
        db '║ configurations. The main configuration that contains the group can also be   ║',10
        db '║ loaded! You can move into any group and (even) come back from it (not like   ║',10
        db '║ with some simular multiple configurations software that I will not mention). ║',10
        db '║ An arrow in the list of configurations indicates that a sub group exists     ║',10
        db '║ under a configuration!                                                       ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²AUTOCONF² has an on-line help, supports an indefinite number of scrollable    ║',10
	db '║ pages for the list of configurations, support 25 and 50 lines modes, loads   ║',10
	db '║ only common part and ends at any moment if demanded.                         ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² has a UNIQUE feature, which you can experience from the list of     ║',10
	db '║ configuration: press TAB to see the configuration itself, including it''s     ║',10
	db '║ name of course. Use arrows to move in your configurations (the one before or ║',10
	db '║ after in the list, alphabetically sorted!), etc...                           ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ More exciting! You can even disable or enable a line in a configuration!     ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² is extremely fast. You will not see any hold up. You startup will   ║',10
	db '║ not seem to be slower! The source code of ²AUTOCONF², written in assembler was ║',10
	db '║ diligently worked in order to have as little useless things as possible!     ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ 15 options of ²AUTOCONF² allow you to personalize ²AUTOCONF² to your real needs. ║',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² is 100% compatible QEMM 7.x, since it''s DOSDATA created lots of     ║',10
        db '║ unbeleivable problems with multiple configuration programs. You can not run  ║',10
	db '║ OPTIMIZE, since it will ignore ²AUTOCONF², which does not take ANY memory, and ║',10
	db '║ run all the configurations one after another.                                ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²AUTOCONF² is fully compatible Windows 95!                                     ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ A silent mode is available! You can make the startup of you computer void    ║',10
	db '║ from any messages from ²AUTOCONF² (except error ones). ²AUTOCONF² supports all   ║',10
	db '║ the keyboards supported by KEYB.COM, 25 lines as well as 50 lines video      ║',10
	db '║ modes are supported, monochrome and CGA supported with no switch options.    ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² does not use any memory!                                            ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ The usage is so simple, you will read this manual only once!                 ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ I could tell you lots of other interesting thing, but I prefer to stop here. ║',10
	db '║                                   Ouf...                                     ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² is totally ²îFREE² for personnal usage only. If you think I do merit   ║',10
	db '║ something, don''t hesitate to thank me financially. A company should be able  ║',10
	db '║ to pay the little I ask, and receive regular upgrades.                       ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ If you want to receive regular upgrades of ²AUTOCONF², please send $10 for     ║',10
	db '║ Switzerland, $20 for Europe and $30 for USA, etc... per year.                ║',10
	db '║ You can call me by modem or send me your favorite BBS number so I can upload ║',10
        db '║ ²AUTOCONF² there!                                                              ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²SINCE ²AUTOCONF² IS FREE, ANY SALE OF ANY VERSION OR ANY PART OF IT IS STRICTLY²║',10
	db '║ ²PROHIBITED. IF YOU WANT TO PERSONALIZE YOUR COPY, JUST ASK FOR REGULAR       ²║',10
	db '║ ²UPGRADES. ANY INDIVUDUAL OR COMPANY WHICH TRIES TO GET ANY BENEFIT FROM THIS ²║',10
	db '║ ²SOFTWARE WITHOUT THE ACCORD OF THE AUTHOR, WILL BE PROSECUTED TO THE MAXIMUM² ║',10
	db '║ ²EXTENT POSSIBLE UNDER THE SWISS CRIMINAL LAW!                               ² ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ Consult WHATSNEW.ENG to see what''s new in this latest version of AUTOCONF!   ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²                       THE COMPLETE MANUAL OF ²AUTOCONF:²                      ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²PARAMETERS FOR CONFIG.SYS²                                                    ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ (you can start an option with / or -)                                        ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/Dx² : the default configuration. This options changes the default config,    ║',10
        db '║       which is loaded if no key is pressed. If you don''t use this option,    ║',10
        db '║       the default value is configuration A.                                  ║',10
        db '║ Note: for function keys configurations (F1...F10) write  /DF1.../DF0.        ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/Hx² : the default configuration for Windows 95.                              ║',10
        db '║       ²AUTOCONF² detects the presence of DOS 7.00, under which Win 95  runs,   ║',10
        db '║       and enables this switch in that case. See the ''Compatibility with      ║',10
        db '║       Windows 95'' below.                                                     ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/T²[²Dx²[²u²]][²Cx²[²u²]]² : the delay for ²AUTOCONF² to wait until a key is pressed.    ║',10
        db '║       You have definetely enough time to choose your configuration before    ║',10
        db '║       ²AUTOCONF² runs, but you may still find this option usefull. The default ║',10
        db '║       is 0 for both DOS and Windows 95.                                      ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ [²D²]: specifies the time to wait under DOS below 7.00.                        ║',10
        db '║ [²C²]: specifies the time to wait under DOS 7.00 and above (Windows 95)        ║',10
        db '║ [²u²]: do not show the pulse while waiting for a key, ex: ²/T5u²                 ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Example: /TD2uC3u forces ²AUTOCONF² to wait 2 seconds under DOS and 3 under    ║',10
        db '║          Windows 95; /T5 forces ²AUTOCONF² to always wait for 5 seconds.       ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: the options'' order is not important, ex: /TC2D4u = /TD4uC2             ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/P² :  silent mode: if you do not like the colorfull messages of ²AUTOCONF²,    ║',10
        db '║       use this option to make them totally dissapear.                        ║',10
        db '║ Note: the list of configurations as well as the manual and all error         ║',10
        db '║       messages will still be shown.                                          ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/N² :  never erase the screen while running ²AUTOCONF.²                         ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/E² :  messages in black and white. If the colorfull messages bother you,     ║',10
	db '║        use this option to disable color, while ²AUTOCONF² runs. This is very   ║',10
	db '║        usefull for LCD screens with a little ammount of gray levels.         ║',10
	db '║        Note: the color toggle in the manual of ²AUTOCONF² can still be used.   ║',10
	db '║        Note: ²AUTOCONF² automatically supports monochrome and CGA.             ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/Kxx² :  used keyboard, where xx:                                             ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║    Belgium                      ²BE²  │ Bresil                       ²BR²        ║',10
	db '║    Canada (french)              ²CF²  │ Tcheckoslovakia (tcheck)     ²CZ²        ║',10
	db '║    Tcheckoslovakia (slovak)     ²SL²  │ Danemark                     ²DK²        ║',10
	db '║    Finland                      ²SU²  │ France                       ²FR²        ║',10
	db '║    Germany                      ²GR²  │ Hungary                      ²HU²        ║',10
	db '║    Italy                        ²IT²  │ Latin America                ²LA²        ║',10
	db '║    Holland                      ²NL²  │ Norvege                      ²NO²        ║',10
	db '║    Poland                       ²PL²  │ Portugal                     ²PO²        ║',10
	db '║    Spain                        ²SP²  │ Sweeden                      ²SV²        ║',10
	db '║    Switzerland (french)         ²SF²  │ Switzerland (german)         ²SG²        ║',10
	db '║    Great Britain                ²UK²  │ Croatia/Serbia/Slovenia      ²YU²        ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ The ²US² keyboard is the one by default.                                       ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/J²[²D²][²C²] : always show the list of configuraitons and prompt for a choice.   ║',10
        db '║ [²D²]: always show the list while booting DOS below 7.00                       ║',10
        db '║ [²C²]: always show the list while booting DOS 7.xx (Windows 95) or above.      ║',10
        db '║      Note: ²/J² alone will set both options.                                   ║',10
        db '║      Note: the order of options is not important, ex: /JCD, /JDC, /JD or /JC.║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ By combining the options ²/Jxx² and ²/Tx², you will get the list of the configs  ║',10
        db '║ during the bootup, that will dissapear to load the default configuration     ║',10
        db '║ after the time, specified by Tx has expired. If you press any key during the ║',10
        db '║ waiting time, the list of configurations will react as usual and void the    ║',10
        db '║ countdown.                                                                   ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/S² : During its execution, ²AUTOCONF² creates ²AUTOCONF.DAT²,                    ║',10
        db '║      which contains a code that designates the configuration chosen. If      ║',10
        db '║      you use this option, the default configration will be the one, chosen   ║',10
        db '║      during the last bootup, which was written in ²AUTOCONF.DAT². That means,  ║',10
        db '║      that it will act as with the ²/D² option: loading if no key is pressed.   ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: ²AUTOCONF.DAT² is always created and modified every time you run         ║',10
        db '║      ²AUTOCONF.² This file is created by iREAD (integrated READCONF) and is    ║',10
        db '║      used by BOOTIT for predefined reboot.                                   ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: This option has no sens if used with ²/J².                               ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/Mx² : During the bootup, ²AUTOCONF² shows a welcome message, which depends of  ║',10
        db '║      the time of the day you are running ²AUTOCONF.² This option allows to     ║',10
        db '║      change these (awesome) messages:                                        ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║            ²/M1² - morning message                                             ║',10
        db '║            ²/M2² - day message                                                 ║',10        
        db '║            ²/M3² - evening message                                             ║',10
        db '║            ²/M4² - night message                                               ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ The same message can be assigned to different hours of the day:              ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/M[xxxx]² : where x is the number of the message.                             ║',10        
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ So if you add an option like:                                                ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║         ²  /M[13]T|he sun is shining#the birds are singing.²                   ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²AUTOCONF² will show this message avery morning or evening:                    ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ ²The sun is shining²                                                           ║',10
	db '║ ²the birds are singing.  ²                                                     ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: each message can have a infinite ammount of caracters which have to    ║',10        
        db '║       be on the same line with DEVICE=AUTOCONF.SYS. The caracter ²|²  is used  ║',10
        db '║       to toggle caps. The caracter ²#² is used to jump a line.                 ║',10
        db '║ Note: if the number of caracters exceeds 77, ²AUTOCONF² will automatically     ║',10
        db '║       jump to the next line.                                                 ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ For example: ²device=AUTOCONF.SYS /M3h|ello dear #|u|ser of |AUTOCONF!     ²   ║',10
        db '║ will show this message on the screen:                                        ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ ²Hello dear²                                                                   ║',10
	db '║ ²User of AUTOCONF!     ²                                                       ║',10        
	db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ Note: if you wish to show the control caracters, such as ²| / - or #,² just    ║',10        
        db '║       write them twice in your message: ²|| // -- ou ##².                      ║',10                
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ ²/Cx² : If you ask for a list of configurations, it has a highlighted line     ║',10        
        db '║       that moves while you press special keys (Home, End, PgUp, PgDn, etc).  ║',10
        db '║       This option allows to change the color of this highlighted line.       ║',10
        db '║       Default is 127.                                                        ║',10
        db '║ ex:² /C}² (Alt 125) will give blue caracters on a gray background.             ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/Fx² : Defines the color of the designations in the configurations list.      ║',10
        db '║       (same syntax as for the ²/Cx² option)                                    ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/G²  : This is an option for those who like to control every little thing.    ║',10
        db '║       Before a list of configuration, a message is showed, telling you what  ║',10
        db '║       keys you can press. This option allows you not to print this message!  ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/5²  : Force a 50 line mode on the screen. That means, ²AUTOCONF² will keep     ║',10        
        db '║       this mode for every screen output and will not remove it after it has  ║',10
        db '║       finished running.                                                      ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/O²  : Compatibility mode with Windows 95, and MS-DOS below version 7.00,     ║',10
        db '║       using QEMM''s DOSDATA. For more detailed information, please consult    ║',10
        db '║       the chapter ''Compatibility with Windows 95'', point 3.                  ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/I²  : Disable the edit mode under the configuration viewer.                  ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/L²  : Always show the configuration name during the bootup.                  ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/B²  : Do not create the hidden AUTOCONF.DAT file, erase if found. /S has no  ║',10
        db '║       sense with this option, but BOOTIT will not be ignored.                ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/Z²  : eLiTe mode! (not for lamers!) ²/ZZ² invert the elite mode.               ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²/V²  : use READCONF instead of iREAD (add READCONF in the AUTOEXEC.BAT file!) ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²STRUCTURE OF CONFIG.SYS       ²                                               ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║²device=[drive][dir]<AUTOCONF.SYS> /[PARAM1] /[PARAM2] ²; call AUTOCONF.        ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║²device=²*²<DESIGNATION> <NAME OF THE CONFIG OF ²THE MAIN GROUP²>²                  ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║        <DESIGNATION> : ²A² for the configuration A, ²F1² for the config F1, etc. ║',10
        db '║        <NAME OF THE CONF> : the name of the configuration, with the char ²|²   ║',10
        db '║                             for caps toggle.                                 ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²device=²**²<DESIGNATION> <NAME OF THE ²SUB² CONFIG> ²                             ║',10
	db '║ ²... configuration ...²                                                        ║',10
        db '║ ²device=²**²<DESIGNATION> <NAME OF THE ²SUB² CONFIG> ²                             ║',10
	db '║ ²... configuration ...²                                                        ║',10
        db '║ ²device=²***²<DESIGNATION> <NAME OF THE ²SUB SUB² CONFIG> ²                        ║',10
	db '║ ²... configuration ...²                                                        ║',10
        db '║ ²device=²*²<DESIGNATION> <NAME OF THE CONFIG OF ²THE MAIN GROUP²>²                 ║',10
        db '║ ²... and so on...        ²                                                     ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: You can create up to 20 configurations'' sub-levels.                    ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: creation of colored configuration names is identical to the procedure  ║',10
        db '║       described for personalized initialisation messages.                    ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: Only the configurations from the main group can be loaded by only      ║',10
        db '║       pressing a key at the bootup, after the Starting DOS message. The sub  ║',10
        db '║       group configurations shall be loaded only from the list of configura-  ║',10
        db '║       tion, obtained with the SPACE BAR at boot.                             ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: The configurations can be put in any order; the list of configurations ║',10
        db '║       will automatically be sorted alphabetically. The extended configs      ║',10
        db '║       (F1 ... F10) will first be shown.                                      ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: If you have not created a default configuration, A, or the one used    ║',10
        db '║       with the /D parameter, an error message will occur.                    ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ Note: If you have created two configurations with the same letter, ex: two   ║',10
        db '║       configurations G, then if you choose a G configuration, both will be   ║',10
        db '║       loaded. This does not apply to sub configurations at all.              ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²device=²$² <------------------------>    ² ; please add any text to this line,  ║',10
        db '║                                         ; in order to let ²AUTOCONF² enough    ║',10
        db '║                                         ; space to add a SET CONF=... line   ║',10
        db '║                                         ; during your computer''s bootup.     ║',10
        db '║ Note: this replaces the READCONF.EXE of the previous versions.               ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ AUTOCONF creates a variable in the master DOS environment, that contains:    ║',10
        db '║ GROUP_CONFIG or simply CONFIG, depending on the choice you have made during  ║',10
        db '║ the bootup. For the config F6, the variable ²CONF² will be set to F6, it will  ║',10
        db '║ become F3_F0_J_L for the configuration L in the sub group J, of the sub      ║',10
        db '║ group F10 of the main group F3.                                              ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²îImportant!² This line must be in the CONFIG.SYS, since it defines the end of  ║',10
        db '║ the multiple configurations. All following lines will become the common part,║',10
        db '║ loaded with every configuration.                                             ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²files=30                              ² ;loaded with every configuration.     ║',10
	db '║ ²buffers=30                            ²                                       ║',10
	db '║ ²lastdrive=E                           ²                                       ║',10
	db '║ ²stacks=9,128                          ²                                       ║',10
        db '║ ²... and so on ...                     ²                                       ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ (full example)                                                               ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ SWITCHES=/F                                                                  ║',10        
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ DEVICE=C:\UTILS\AUTOCONF.SYS /KSF /DF1 /F /5                                ║',10        
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ device=**F2 P|rogramming                                                     ║',10        
        db '║  device=c:\dos\himem.sys /testmem:off                                        ║',10        
        db '║  devicehigh=c:\dos\setver.exe                                                ║',10        
        db '║  devicehigh=c:\dos\ansi.sys                                                  ║',10        
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ device=*F1 DOS                                                               ║',10        
        db '║  device=c:\dos\himem.sys /testmem:off                                        ║',10        
        db '║  device=c:\dos\emm386.exe ram                                                ║',10        
        db '║  devicehigh=c:\utils\mtm\mtmcdai.sys /d:MTMIDE01                             ║',10        
        db '║  devicehigh=c:\dos\ansi.sys                                                  ║',10        
        db '║  shell=c:\dos\command.com /p                                                 ║',10        
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║    device=**F0 DOS                                                           ║',10        
        db '║         device=c:\dos\himem.sys /testmem:off                                 ║',10        
        db '║         device=c:\dos\emm386.exe RAM                                         ║',10        
        db '║         devicehigh=c:\dos\ansi.sys                                           ║',10 
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║    device=**F1 HIMEM/EMM386 (NOEMS)                                          ║',10        
        db '║         device=c:\dos\himem.sys /testmem:off                                 ║',10        
        db '║         device=c:\dos\emm386.exe NOEMS                                       ║',10        
        db '║         devicehigh=c:\dos\ansi.sys                                           ║',10        
        db '║         shell=c:\4dos\4dos.com /p                                            ║',10        
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ device=*W W|indows| (N|o| NETWORK)                                           ║',10        
        db '║         device=c:\dos\himem.sys /TESTMEM:OFF                                 ║',10        
        db '║         devicehigh=c:\utils\mtm\MTMCDAI.SYS /D:MTMIDE01                      ║',10        
        db '║         device=c:\dos\ansi.sys                                               ║',10        
        db '║         SHELL=C:\4DOS\4DOS.COM /P                                            ║',10        
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ device=$ <--------------------------->                                       ║',10        
        db '║                                                                              ║',10        
        db '║ buffers=40                                                                   ║',10        
        db '║ files=40                                                                     ║',10        
        db '║ dos=high,umb                                                                 ║',10        
        db '║ devicehigh=c:\dos\setver.exe                                                 ║',10        
        db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²STRUCTURE OF THE AUTOEXEC.BAT² (multiple configurations)                      ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²goto %conf%              ²  ;jump to the chosen configuration                 ║',10
        db '║ ²goto def_conf            ²  ;in case the name of the config is invalid, go to ║',10        
        db '║                                ;the default configuration                    ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²:def_conf      ²            ;configuration A, the default one (my choice)     ║',10
	db '║ ²:A             ²            ;configuration A                                  ║',10
	db '║ ²...configuration...²                                                          ║',10
        db '║ ²goto end      ²             ;jump to the end of AUTOEXEC.BAT                  ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²:<DESIGNATION>[[_<SUB CONF>]_<SUB CONF>]  ²                                   ║',10
        db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║                            ;is the general syntax; for the sub-configuration ║',10
        db '║                            ;F8 under the configuration F1, for instance,     ║',10
        db '║                            ;simply specify F1_F8. For more inforamtion on    ║',10
        db '║                            ;this option, please consult the point concerning ║',10
        db '║                            ;the CONF variable one page higher.               ║',10
        db '║ ²goto end      ²             ;jump to the end of AUTOEXEC.BAT                  ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ ²:end          ²             ;COMMON part                                      ║',10
	db '║ ²...           ²             ;PROMPT=..., PATH=..., etc...                     ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²KEYS                        ²                                                 ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²ON-LINE HELP, obtained with BACKSPACE everywhere except under TAB:  ²         ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²ARROWS UP AND LEFT   ²one line up                                             ║',10
	db '║ ²       RIGHT, DOWN   ²one line down                                           ║',10
	db '║ ²PAGE DOWN            ²next page                                               ║',10
	db '║ ²PAGE UP              ²one page up                                             ║',10
	db '║ ²ESCAPE               ²quit the help file                                      ║',10
	db '║ ²SPACE                ²toggle color - b/w modes                                ║',10
	db '║ ²TAB                  ²toggle 25/50 lines modes                                ║',10
        db '║ ²INSERT               ²search for a string                                     ║',10
        db '║ ²DELETE               ²cancel search mode                                      ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²THE LIST OF CONFIGS, obtained with SPACE instead of choosing a configuration:²║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²BACKSPACE            ²show the on-line help                                   ║',10
        db '║ ²SPACE of ENTER       ²load the highlighted configuration                      ║',10
        db '║ ²ARROWS UP            ²scroll up in the list                                   ║',10
        db '║ ²       DOWN          ²scroll to the next configuration in the list            ║',10
        db '║ ²       LEFT          ²show the subgroup of the configuration if exists        ║',10
        db '║ ²       RIGHT         ²show the upper level of the group                       ║',10
        db '║ (If you are in the main group or there''s no sub level, the last two keys are ║',10
        db '║  simply ignored and a short beep is emitted)                                 ║',10
	db '║ ²HOME & PAGE UP       ²the first configuration on the screen                   ║',10
	db '║ ²END & PAGE DOWN      ²last configuration on screen                            ║',10
        db '║ ²TAB                  ²show the highlighted configuration                      ║',10
        db '║ ²STAR                 ²end ²AUTOCONF²                                            ║',10
	db '║ ²POINT                ²load only the common part                               ║',10
        db '║ Any other key designating a configuration, loads it, if it exists.           ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²THE CONFIGURATION ITSELF SHOWED with TAB from the list of configurations:    ²║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²ARROWS:              ²                                                        ║',10
        db '║ ²UP                   ²scroll the configuration up (if longer than 25 lines)   ║',10
        db '║ ²DOWN                 ²scroll the configuration down (if longer than 25 lines) ║',10
        db '║ ²RIGHT                ²scroll the configuration to the right                   ║',10
        db '║ ²LEFT                 ²scroll the configuration to the left                    ║',10
        db '║ ²HOME                 ²jump to the beginning of the line                       ║',10
        db '║                      if any of the shown lines exceeds 80 characters         ║',10
	db '║ ²PAGE DOWN            ²next configuration                                      ║',10
	db '║ ²PAGE UP              ²previous configuration in list                          ║',10
	db '║ ²TAB, ESC             ²return to the list of configurations                    ║',10
	db '║ ²SPACE                ²toggle color - b/w modes                                ║',10
	db '║ ²ENTER                ²choose the shown configuration                          ║',10
        db '║ ²POINT (.)            ²load only the common part, after device=$               ║',10
        db '║ ²BACKSPACE            ²show the on-line help                                   ║',10
        db '║ ²E (E key)            ²enable/disable line editing mode                        ║',10
        db '║ ²  SPACE in ''E'' mode  ²enable/disable a line                                   ║',10
        db '║ ²      ? in ''E'' mode  ²enable/disable execute the line prompt                  ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²COMPATIBILITY WITH WINDOWS 95!                     ²                          ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ Version 2.6+ fully supports Windows 95.                                      ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ That means:                                                                  ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ 1. General Idea:                                                             ║',10
        db '║ While booting Win 95, you get two choices, use Windows 95 OS or your old     ║',10
	db '║ DOS. F4 will load DOS and anything else, Windows 4.0... The SHELL= parameter ║',10
	db '║ allows to choose a different OS commander, like COMMAND.COM of DOS below 7.0 ║',10
	db '║ or 4DOS.                                                                     ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ Old 16 bit and DOS programs still need more memory, and of course multiple   ║',10
        db '║ configurations. ²AUTOCONF² will check for Win 95, so when you run Windows 95,  ║',10
	db '║ the option /Dx will be ignored, but the /Hx, encounted (if both, of course,  ║',10
        db '║ are present). That allows you to create a special configuration for Win 95   ║',10
	db '║ and another one for DOS below 7.0, without having to choose another config   ║',10
	db '║ every time!                                                                  ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ 2. ²AUTOCONF² will force the screen to switch from the Win 95 initialisation   ║',10
	db '║ screen to normal DOS loading sheme. That will help you see what''s happening  ║',10
	db '║ behind that nice drawing and fully use ²AUTOCONF²!                             ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ 3. Windows 95, DOS and QEMM 7.x DOSDATA:                                     ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ If you are using configurations with QEMM''s DOSDATA you are normally forced  ║',10
	db '║ to do the following:                                                         ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║      # press F4 to run MS-DOS                                                ║',10
        db '║      # choose a configuration with ²AUTOCONF² containing DOSDATA               ║',10
	db '║      # press F4 again, since the CONFIG.SYS is reinitialized by DOSDATA      ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ With option ²/O²:                                                              ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
        db '║ The last step is supressed by ²AUTOCONF² 2.61+. You just press F4 to load DOS, ║',10
	db '║ then you choose the configuration with AUTOCONF.                             ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ Note: some older BIOSs will not support this function.                       ║',10
	db '║                                                                              ║',10
	db '║ Note: the F4 key is simulated in any case, except when you want to run       ║',10
        db '║       Windows 95. If DOSDATA is not present, a beep will occur at the end of ║',10  
	db '║       the bootup, since the computer keeps the "pressed" key until the DOS   ║',10
	db '║       prompt. A small utility has been added: CLRBUF.SYS and CLRBUF.COM,     ║',10
	db '║       which erase the keyboard buffer and supress this beep. CLRBUF does not ║',10
	db '║       take memory and does not print anything on the screen. Use CLRBUF.SYS  ║',10
	db '║       in the common part of the CONFIG.SYS file, or CLRBUF.COM in the common ║',10
	db '║       part of the AUTOEXEC.BAT.                                              ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²IMPORTANT NOTE FOR WINDOWS 95 SUPPORT: ²                                      ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²AUTOCONF² 2.90 has been tested with Windows 95, final version of 24th august. ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²IMPORTANT NOTES:  ²                                                           ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ The line: DOS=[high],[UMB] is read only once in the CONFIG.SYS file. The     ║',10
	db '║ last occurence will only be taken in consideration by DOS. ²AUTOCONF² can not  ║',10        
        db '║ do anything for the choice of where to load DOS, high or low.                ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
        db '║ ²AUTOCONF², version 1.1 to this latter, all versions of ²READCONF², ²i²R²E²A²D² and    ║',10
        db '║ ²BOOTIT² are the property of (me):                                             ║',10
        db '║ ²▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄ ²Doubrovkine Daniel      ²                                         ║',10
        db '║ ²████³███²████ ²11, ch. de la Clairière ²                                         ║',10
	db '║ ²██³███████²██ ²1207 Genève,            ²                                         ║',10
	db '║ ²████³███²████ ²Suisse                  ²                                         ║',10
        db '║ ²▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀ ²tel & fax: 41 22 - 735 69 47       ²                              ║',10
        db '║ ²email: dblock@infomaniak.ch                      ²                            ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²AUTOCONF² was originally programmed by a french coder which is unknown to me. ║',10
	db '║ A version, that I used as the engine of ²AUTOCONF² was published in a SVM,     ║',10
	db '║ several years ago. 90% of the original program, have been modified. The name ║',10
        db '║ has not been changed.                                                        ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ I thank all the beta testers and all those who took any part in the develop- ║',10
	db '║ pement of this software.                                                     ║',10
	db '╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣',10
	db '║ ²All the names of companies, as well as their products are the trademarks of  ²║',10
	db '║ ²their respectif oweners.                           ²                          ║',10
	db '╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝',10
	db '²[                              end of help                                     '
			     
press_a_extended_key db '²?[²  ²?line² HOME ²?beginning² END ²? ² PgUp PgDn ²?page² ESPACE ²?color/b&w² TAB ²?50/25² ESC ²?]'
